  "database": "rschema_0375",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0375 database is designed to manage and track various aspects of devices and their interactions with users. The Device table stores information about each device, including its status, name, type, IP address, installation location, installation time, and ID, which serves as the primary key. The User table contains details about users, such as their ID and password, while the Staff table holds information about staff members, including their ID and name. The Network_Traffic table tracks network traffic data for each device, including download and upload traffic, timestamp, and status, with a composite primary key consisting of the device ID and timestamp, and a foreign key referencing the Device table to establish the relationship between network traffic and the device it belongs to. The Device_Failure_Record table stores records of device failures, including the device ID, failure description, occurrence time, type, handling status, and remarks, with a composite primary key of device ID and failure occurrence time, and a foreign key referencing the Device table to link the failure record to the device it pertains to. The User_Connection_Device table tracks user connections to devices, including connection and disconnection times, used bandwidth, user ID, and user IP, with a composite primary key of user ID, device ID, and connection time, and foreign keys referencing the User and Device tables to establish relationships between users, devices, and their connections. The Device_Maintenance_Record table stores maintenance records for devices, including device ID, maintenance content, result, time, and remarks, with a composite primary key of device ID, staff ID, and maintenance time, and foreign keys referencing the Device and Staff tables to link the maintenance record to the device and staff member involved.",
  "gold_question": "The wireless network monitoring and device management system primarily functions to manage device information, record network traffic data, track device failures and maintenance status, and monitor user connections to devices. The system is also capable of tracking maintenance operations performed by staff on the devices. The database includes the following functions:\n\nDevice Management: record basic information of all network devices. Fields include Device ID, Name, Type, IP Address, Installation Location, Installation Time, and Device Status. \n \nUser Management: store user account information. Fields include User ID, User Account, and User Password. \n \nNetwork traffic Management: record network traffic data of each device at specific time points. Fields include Device ID, Timestamp, Upload Traffic, Download Traffic, Total Traffic, and Traffic Status.  \n\nDevice failure record Management: record device failure information. Fields include Device ID, Failure Occurrence Time, Failure Type, Failure Description, Handling Status, and Remarks.  \n\nStaff Management: record information about staff members. Fields include Staff ID, Name, and Contact Information.  \n\nUser connection device Management: record the connection status between users and devices. Fields include User ID, Device ID, Connection Time, Disconnection Time, Bandwidth Used, and User IP.  \n\nDevice maintenance record Management: Used to document device maintenance information. Fields include Device ID, Staff ID, Maintenance Time, Maintenance Content, Maintenance Result, and Remarks.  \n\nThe design of thus system is primarily for device management, network traffic monitoring, failure diagnosis and handling, tracking user connection status, and maintaining device maintenance records.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0375.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0375\nCREATE TABLE `device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `installation_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `installation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `staff` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `network_traffic` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `download_traffic` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `upload_traffic` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`, `timestamp`),\n  CONSTRAINT `network_traffic_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_failure_record` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `failure_occurrence_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `failure_description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `handling_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`, `failure_occurrence_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_failure_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_connection_device` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `connection_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `disconnection_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `used_bandwidth` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `user_ip` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `device_id`, `connection_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_connection_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_connection_device_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_maintenance_record` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_content` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `result` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`, `staff_id`, `maintenance_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
